{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Observation and Outcome Periods.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Observation and Outcome Periods.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"observation and outcome periods observation and outcome periods","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Observation and Outcome Periods.md","fileName":"Observation and Outcome Periods.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Observation and Outcome Periods","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 09:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Data Science Deployment and Renewal]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Science Deployment and Renewal","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Observation and Outcome Periods.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Observation and Outcome Periods.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"observation and outcome periods observation and outcome periods","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Observation and Outcome Periods.md","fileName":"Observation and Outcome Periods.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Observation and Outcome Periods","heading":"Observation and Outcome Periods","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"In a propensity model, the observation period supplies the input attributes, while a later outcome period determines whether the predicted event occurred. The interval between them defines how far ahead the prediction is meant to work.\n\nFor churn, a model intended to warn two months before departure must train on information that would have been available two months before each historic customer's departure. Using later activity in the inputs would create a misleadingly easy task and leave too little time for an actual retention intervention.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Science Deployment and Renewal","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart